YOU MAY

- Download, install and use Blip on your own computers, for any purpose,
  including at work.
- Make the copies that come with normal use: installing, building and
  updating Blip (for example git clone, git pull or a Claude Code plugin
  install), and backing up or syncing your own copy between your own
  computers.
- Read the code, link to this repository, and use an AI assistant (such as
  Claude Code) to install, run, read or work on Blip for the uses allowed
  here.
- Suggest changes: fork this repository on GitHub, change your fork, and
  send the changes back as a pull request, or describe them in a GitHub
  issue.


CONTRIBUTIONS

When you send a change, you confirm that you have the right to send it, and
you allow Mohamed to use, change, publish and license it as part of Blip,
under these terms or any later terms Mohamed chooses.


YOU MAY NOT, WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM MOHAMED

- Copy the code, in whole or in part, into another project.
- Publish, share or sell a changed version of the code or of the app, other
  than a fork used only to send a pull request to this repository.
- Share, publish or sell copies of the code or of the app. Share a link to
  this repository instead.
- Use the code, the Sprout character or this repository to train, fine-tune
  or evaluate AI models, or include them in any dataset. Using an AI
  assistant as allowed above is not training.

A fork of this repository on GitHub, which GitHub's Terms of Service allow,
is only for viewing the code and sending pull requests. It does not allow
any of the things listed under YOU MAY NOT.


